========================================
SERVICE: AUTH SERVICE
========================================

PURPOSE:
Handles authentication and authorization using JWT-based stateless security.

----------------------------------------
CORE RESPONSIBILITIES:
----------------------------------------
- User Registration
- User Login
- Password Encryption (BCrypt)
- JWT Token Generation
- Role Management (USER / ADMIN)

----------------------------------------
FEATURES IMPLEMENTED:
----------------------------------------

1. USER REGISTRATION
- Accepts name, email, password
- Encrypts password using BCrypt
- Stores user in DB
- Assigns default role: USER

2. USER LOGIN
- Validates email and password
- Uses CustomUserDetailsService
- Generates JWT token on success

3. JWT TOKEN GENERATION
- Subject: email
- Claims: role
- Expiry: configurable
- Signed using secret key

4. ROLE MANAGEMENT
- Enum-based roles: USER, ADMIN
- Used for authorization

5. CUSTOM USER DETAILS SERVICE
- Fetches user from database
- Converts UserEntity → Spring Security User

6. PASSWORD SECURITY
- BCrypt hashing
- Secure password comparison

----------------------------------------
API CONTRACTS:
----------------------------------------

POST /auth/register
Request:
- name
- email
- password

POST /auth/login
Request:
- email
- password

Response:
- token (JWT)

----------------------------------------
DATABASE:
----------------------------------------

TABLE: users
- id
- name
- email (unique)
- password
- role

----------------------------------------
SECURITY DESIGN:
----------------------------------------
- Stateless authentication
- No session storage
- JWT-based access control

----------------------------------------
TECH STACK:
----------------------------------------
- Spring Boot 3.5.13
- Spring Security
- JPA + MySQL
- JWT (jjwt 0.11.5)

----------------------------------------
ERROR HANDLING:
----------------------------------------
- Invalid credentials → Exception
- User not found → Exception
- Handled via GlobalExceptionHandler

----------------------------------------
LOGGING:
----------------------------------------
- Login attempts
- Authentication failures

----------------------------------------
SUMMARY:
----------------------------------------
Auth Service manages user authentication and generates JWT tokens
to enable secure, stateless communication across microservices.